R1c0_qkvza_intraquad_softpipe kernel=fused_qkvza_hfq4g256 lever=intraquad_softpipe verdict=DEAD delta_pct=0.16 f=0.375 learned=Intra-quad header softpipe raised VGPR 72->88 (compiler kept current+next live) and lifted occ 35->47.7% / mem_busy 41->58.4% while L2 fell 77.6->61.2%; throughput flat (delta +0.16%, f=0.375). Confirms qkvza is TLP-hidden not MLP-limited — schedule reordering cannot unlock wall time; need a non-MLP lever (cheaper VALU/dual-issue or real cache policy), not more pipelining.
R10c3_rms_ready_wavepoll kernel=fused_rmsnorm_mq_rotate lever=rms_ready_wavepoll verdict=DEAD delta_pct=-0.22 f=0.5 learned=Replacing the second full-block barrier with one shared ready flag polled by lane 0 of each wave raised VGPR 48->56 while occupancy remained structurally capped at 0.2%; with parity intact and no throughput lift, barrier release is not the limiting latency and atomic wave polling only adds register pressure.
